>
  <h2>Why don’t you accept donations?</h2>
  <p>doorbell.life is currently run by its maintainer as an individual, and no formal organization has been set up yet. Until then, we won’t ask the public for money in the name of a good cause, and the site has no donation feature. If anyone asks you to donate to doorbell.life, it isn’t us.</p>

  <h2>Where does income come from?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Corporate sponsorship, as part of a company’s ESG efforts. See <a href="/about/usa/sponsors/">For corporate sponsors</a>.</li>
    <li>Ads: article pages on this site will show Google AdSense ads.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where will there never be ads?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Anything doorbell.life shows on other websites’ error pages.</li>
    <li>The error page templates we provide.</li>
    <li>Every page about missing persons.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where does the money go?</h2>
  <p>Our only fixed cost is the doorbell.life domain, at US$28.20 a year. The website, data files, and widget all run on Cloudflare’s free plan. We make everything we can into static files precisely so costs stay within the free tier.</p>
</AboutPage>
